o} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412401}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c2f8794d-09da-5fac-b8f1-8d4a0461ec58" :question/math-academy-id "q-82021" :question/problem "Rewrite the statement $¬((¬X∨Y)∧(¬Y∨X))$ using De Morgan's laws." :question/worked-solution "De Morgan's laws state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(X∧Y)≡¬X∨¬Y, \\\\ ¬(X∨Y)≡¬X∧¬Y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can simplify the given statement as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬((¬X∨Y)∧(¬Y∨X)) & ≡¬(¬X∨Y)∨¬(¬Y∨X) \\\\  & ≡(¬(¬X)∧¬Y)∨(¬(¬Y)∧¬X) \\\\  & ≡(X∧¬Y)∨(Y∧¬X)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
